    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity to `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, keeping structural impact to **2 files**, both small classes with little surrounding complexity.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (rewritten `service`) \u2014 now builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n- REGION = `Locality.of(city, postcode)` (postcode-derived region, city fallback) \u2014 reuses the existing region logic.\n- HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (telephone is already E.164-normalized upstream in the pipeline).\n- The old `OwnerRepository` dependency and per-city sequence count are gone \u2014 the sequence is dropped entirely.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (one `@Mapping` line) \u2014 `locality` now derives from the customerCode's REGION component instead of independently from city+postcode, so the locality derivation moves onto the new identity.\n\n**Everything downstream followed automatically** because it already reads `customerCode`:\n- `membershipNumber` (`customerCode + \"-M\" + year`) and `checkDigit` (Luhn over the code's digits) in the mapper now compute over the region-hash code.\n- The `LogAuditOnCreate` audit record logs the new `customerCode`.\n\nNo YAML/wiring changes were needed \u2014 OfficeFloor resolves the trimmed parameter list by injection. Verified via the audit line `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E` and a green build (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`).\n\nNote: seed owners have null `customerCode`/`registrationDate` and the mapper already dereferences `registrationDate.getYear()`, so only pipeline-created owners are ever serialized \u2014 the new `customerCode.substring(...)` in the locality mapping is safe for every owner that actually reaches the mapper.",
